      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-134976",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following polynomial identity for natural $x$ and $y$:\n\n$(x^{2}\u2013y^{2})^{2} + (2xy)^{2} = (x^{2} + y^{2})^{2}$\n\nWhen $x = p$ and $y = q$ are substituted into this identity, they generate the Pythagorean triple $(10, 24, 26)$. What is the value of $p + q$?"
